{"qid":"Q2723760","names":["Giudicato of Gallura"],"title":"Giudicato of Gallura","endonym":null,"capsule":"The Giudicato of Gallura was the northeastern of Sardinia's four medieval judicates — indigenous sovereign polities that emerged from Byzantine administrative units after the Arab disruption of central Mediterranean authority around the ninth century. Its capital was Civita (Olbia), and its rulers bore the title of iudex (judge). From the twelfth century the judicate fell under increasing Pisan influence through marriage alliances, eventually passing to the Visconti of Pisa in 1207. The Aragonese conquest of Sardinia in 1323–1324 extinguished Pisan authority, and the judicate form was never revived.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. The existence of the four Sardinian judicates is well attested in medieval charters and chronicles, but exact territorial boundaries of Gallura vis-à-vis the other judicates are incompletely mapped.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Judicate of Gallura","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Judicate_of_Gallura"},{"label":"Britannica: Sardinia — history","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Sardinia/History"}],"britannica":null,"cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Judicate of Gallura","rulers":[{"qid":null,"name":"Manfredi","nativeName":"","roman":"Manfredi","start":1020,"end":1040,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Baldo","nativeName":"","roman":"Baldo","start":1040,"end":1065,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Costantino I","nativeName":"","roman":"Costantino I","start":1065,"end":1080,"image":